    "body": "## DUNCAN PRIME — PACK SUFFICIENCY / EXECUTION ROUTE CORRECTION R01\n\nCURRENT_MAIN = `b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1`\nTRACKER = #248\nPURPOSE = stop stale source/Krita loop and distinguish reference sufficiency from witness/rig readiness\n\n### FRESH FINDING\n`FULL_CHARACTER_MODEL_LOCK_R02 = PASS` remains authoritative from #245.\n\nThe verified physical `ZORR_CHARACTER_PRO_PACK_R01.zip` contains 6/6 valid sheets with matching manifest hashes: head pitch/volume, body construction, hair topology, hands canon, hand expression, face acting. The same audit also locked the accepted authority split using suit turnaround, head yaw and costume/accessory references.\n\nCurrent #248 source recovery evidence additionally has exact accepted C00 source identities for:\n- MASTER FRONT = `57fbec5d9c136a90c6ac262f8011665fa061dca427bf3fb2c3f110d1cb0a69ed`\n- BODY TURNAROUND = `49f1c5fa9973f185c4ed7441325e2705d392449f6d59b4592ec6d81bc4b4da82`\n- COSTUME / ACCESSORY = `94c185aea5755e569f8359fd29c6e0b8a1748e1613f2b59e7a3e280205dcbc8e`\n\n### IMPORTANT CONTRACT CORRECTION\nThe frozen `COSTUME_MECHANICS_R01_WITNESS_EXECUTION_PROTOCOL_R01.md` requires W01 to remain bounded by accepted character authorities and pass the attachment/fold/body/costume/no-redesign matrix. It does **not** require the whole pack to be physically co-opened in one editor, and it does **not** require `KRITA_CONSUMED_EXACT_SOURCE` as a product acceptance criterion.\n\nIssue #231 production law is also explicit: strong pose/head/acting changes come from **new key drawings**; one raster is not stretched into every pose. Therefore the later `exact MASTER FRONT -> Krita direct edit` binding route was a verification mechanism, not the definition of W01, and must not remain a blocker after it failed to advance the product.\n\n### SUFFICIENCY MATRIX\n- `CHARACTER_IDENTITY_REFERENCE_SUFFICIENT_FOR_W01 = YES`\n- `BODY_REFERENCE_SUFFICIENT_FOR_W01 = YES`\n- `HAND_REFERENCE_SUFFICIENT_FOR_W01 = YES`\n- `COSTUME_ATTACHMENT / SILHOUETTE AUTHORITY_SUFFICIENT_FOR_W01 = YES` (from accepted audit + C00 costume/master/turnaround + locked control matrix)\n- `W01_VALID_WITNESS_ARTIFACT = NO`\n- `W01 = NOT PASS`\n- `W02..W06 = CLOSED`\n- `SEPARATED_OPENTOONZ_SOURCE = NOT READY`, but this is a **later rig/animation readiness gap**, not a W01 reference-pack blocker.\n\n### WHY PRIOR FRAMES DID NOT ADVANCE #248\nA prior W01 visual attempt exists durably and failed. The exact source set was recovered, but the produced output was an unrelated QA/report-board image with a different character/costume; its own matrix failed body model, costume model, ivory/black hierarchy, no-redesign and framing. That is a failed W01 witness, not evidence that the character pack is missing.\n\n### RETIRE THESE AS CURRENT W01 BLOCKERS\n- generic BODY/HAIR/HANDS research\n- rebuilding `ZORR_CHARACTER_PRO_PACK_R01`\n- source-pack rediscovery from zero\n- Krita binding as a mandatory W01 product gate\n- direct raster retargeting as the only legal W01 method\n\n### FIRST REAL BLOCKER NOW\n`VALID_W01_ARM_RAISE_KEY_DRAWING/WITNESS_NOT_YET_PRODUCED_AND_PASSED`\n\n### NEXT PRODUCT STEP\nAuthor/produce **one new W01 ARM_RAISE key drawing/witness** from the already-accepted multi-reference character authority, preserving the locked W01 mechanics. Then persist the actual artifact + SHA256 + full W01 matrix and run independent QC.\n\nNo W02+. No character redesign. No new framework/editor/runner. Do not reopen pack sufficiency unless fresh contradictory evidence appears.",
